The diffs for patch kit 3 are being mailed tonight to
comp.sources.games, and they will be posted there -- I'm
sure -- fairly promptly.

There are two much discussed items which are NOT part of
the patch, and I thought that an explanation is in order.

We did not make changes in the open/closed doors graphics.
We looked carefully at suggestions posted here, at proposals
mailed to us, or otherwise delivered to us.  A couple of
these proposals are very reasonable, if only rooms are taken
into consideration.  The difficulty is -- and that was missed
in most of the proposals -- that a map location "eaten" up
by moles, etc, also uses the doorway code and graphics.  Think
of an area next to a room "eaten" up by moles.  What is it to
be?  A floor area continuous with the room's, but without
walls marking its boundary?  The point is that a change in the
open door graphics requires compehensive evaluatio.    We
decided to postpone such an evaluation until the game has been
debugged.

Another much maligned feature we have not yet touched is the
"eat" code.  Here there are no conceptual difficulties:  we all
agree that eating must use the timeout code.  We even got a very
nice first pass at it from Don Reese.  The eating timeout patch
is being prepared by Mike Stephenson, but his work on it was
blissfully interrupted by his wedding (:-)).  He is back now, and
the eating timeout patch will most probably be part of patch 4 in
the near future.  Some of the features of Don Reese's proposal will
be incorporated

Also part of patch 4 will be a VMS port.  We are still after bugs,
and we credit you with the increasing cleanliness of the code.

For the development team,

